  "_title": "A calculator with no computer in it",
  "_description": "Set A on one switch bank and B on the other; the 74HC283 adds them and the CD4511 turns the 4-bit answer into a decimal digit on the display. There is no CPU, no firmware and nothing to program — the answer is the wiring. Sums of 10 to 15 blank the display: a BCD decoder only knows 0-9, and that honest limit is the reason real adders carry a \"decimal adjust\" stage.",
  "_category": "logic",
  "_difficulty": 5,
  "_stage": "L7"
